  n=24 gives the Golay octad number 759; n=72 gives 249849.
  The scalar gate stays open through this ladder; support realization is separate.

[3] Cross-domain reading
  eta^1: sparse infinite product gate -> partition reciprocal.
  eta^3: Jacobi triangular gate -> still sparse, now weighted by 2k+1.
  eta^24: Delta gate -> dense tau coefficients but modularly controlled.
  Type II W_n: finite invariant-ring gate -> low-weight zeros by Gleason.
  Tutte/Greene direction: code weight enumerators are matroid partition
  functions, so support realization should be audited as a matroid gate,
  not just as a polynomial gate.
